Benjie Gandionco <benjieg@corp.nsc.com> wrote in article 
> I accidently overwrote the existing root crontab file on our AS 2100. 
How
> can I restore it?  We have anther DU on an AS600.  Can I just copy the
root
> crontab file from there?
> 
> Thanks,
> Benjie
> 
> 

Dear Mr.Benjie

	You can restore the root crontab file from a backup copy(available on
your other m/c AS 600), by doing the following

1) Login as root on the machine that lost the root crontab file
2) # crontab -e
3) :r savecopy   <inside vi>
4) :wq		<inside vi>

crontab -e basically allows you to edit the crontab file of the logged user
and throws up a vi session. So just restore it by reading in the backup
file and saving it.

5)# crontab -l  
This will list out all the crontab entries for your verfication. You can
change 
them if you want, by running crontab -e again.

Hope this info helps you

Sincerely

Sukumar Alagappan
