I'm having a problem getting a DEC laser 2100 (w/ PS) to run as a serial
printer on a DEC 3000 AXP 400.  I used lprsetup to generate the printcap
entry, and have tried both /dev/tty00 and 01, along with various cables
and crossovers (but finally matched pins, so my current cable goes 1-1
and 14-14, etc.).  Baud rate and other parm's on the printer match what
is set in printcap:

ps06|lp|lp0|ps0|postscript|PostScript:\
        :br#9600:\
        :ct=dev:\
        :fc#0177777:\
        :fs#03:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/ln05rof:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/ps06-err:\
        :lp=/dev/tty01:\
        :mx#0:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/ln05rof:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#80:\
        :sh:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/ps06:\
        :xc#0177777:\
        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:\
        :xs#044000:

Note that I removed the :rw: entry that lprsetup generates.  I tried it
that way, too, but noticed it screws things up for the parallel setup.

The spool directory and error log exist and have the correct permissions
(matched to a working parallel printer on another machine).

Dave Rainwater
rain@pheno.physics.wisc.edu
