We're having trouble with the utmp file on our dec 4710 
alpha system running osf/1 3.0.

Every few minutes a file /var/adm/utmp.lck appears, which seems to
be hard-linked to /var/adm/utmp. While this file exists (always
between 45 and 90 seconds) all login and logout attempts are blocked.

It looks like a file lock is put on /var/adm/utmp for about a minute
after users logout from telnet or rlogin sessions. This doesnt happen
with every logout, maybe about 1 in 10 - often enough to be a major
nuisance.

