Hello,

   I have been experiencing the following problem, and am running out of
   avenues to follow. 

   I am using a Dec Alpha running OSF1 unix, and have an application which
   is attempting to use Packet filtering to communicate with an existing
   application Dec PDP11, running a proprietry real-time operating system.

   The problem arises with the Packet Filtering due to the style of ethernet
   addressing, used on the proprietry PDP11 methods. The PDP11, uses
   physical Ethernet Addresses which are Multicast. 

   This at first appearances is not unusual, the application running on the
   Dec Alpha can filter on multicast (Destination) addresses using promiscuous
   and copyall filtering options, and this is true for packets which contain a
   destination Ethernet Address with the Multicast Ethernet Bit set.

   However, the problem arrises through the style of ethernet address used
   by the PDP11 system with which communication is attempted. Because the
   physical address of the DP11 machine also has the multicast bit set,
   this means that both destination and source addresses in the received
   packet on the Dec Alpha are multicast in nature.

   Through investigation to date, I have established definately that the Kernel
   is rejecting received packets with a source address that has the multicast
   address bit set.

   Can anybody suggest, software / operating system options which I could
   use to overcom this problem. Any sugestions are welcome. Currently I
   am looking into low level ethernet hardware configuration (at register
   level for the device driver - if possible). 

