Subject: Re: ifconfig: IP aliases
Date: 1996/10/31
Message-ID: <55ai6o$138@tom.amherst.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 193432845
references: <32778FE0.783C@wrc.noaa.gov>
organization: Amherst College, Amherst MA, USA
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Tina Stewart (stewart@wrc.noaa.gov) wrote:
: Hello,

: I've defined multiple IP aliases for an FDDI card in a DEC Alpha 400
: running OSF/1 3.2.

: How does one keep these addresses defined through machine reboots and
: network service restarts?

You probably want to edit your /etc/rc.config file to look something
like this,

NUM_NETCONFIG="2"
NETDEV_0="ln0"
NETDEV_1="ln0"
IFCONFIG_0="148.85.1.54 netmask 255.255.0.0"
IFCONFIG_1="148.85.124.10 netmask 255.255.0.0"

Note the NUM_NETCONFIG entry.

I've found this solution more successful that using the alias
construction.

