In article <541a7s$9mm@stc06.ctd.ornl.gov>, xgz@gmsds.ms.ornl.gov 
(Xiaoguang Zhang) writes:
|>We have just bought several Alpha clones running Digital Unix 4.0.
|>We encountered a strange problem when testing these machines. On
|>two of them if we run a fortran program compiled with the compiler
|>switch "-fast" or "-mathlib fast" then the system crashes. On two
|>other machines the same program runs with no problem. The only
|>difference between these machines are the ones that crashed have
|>a few more options installed. Is this a bug in the OS? How can I
|>get it fixed? Any help is appreciated.

I have never heard of a problem where using the -mathlib fast option would
cause the system to crash.  There could be some sort of timing problem in
the machines.  I think you'll have to try a bit harder to narrow down the
problem (can you find the one option, which when installs, triggers the
problem?) 

We don't test Digital Fortran using non-Digital systems.  In general, if
the base operating system claims support of the configuration, we'll support
it as well, but if we can't reproduce the problem on our own systems.  You
might want to enlist the assistance of the system vendor.
