>I purchased an Alpha workstation 500/333 from an Alpha clone company (they
>purchase the chip/motherboard from Digital, then build the system) and I am
>trying to upgrade the firmware with the CD that came with Digital UNIX 4.0A. 
>The minimum listed firmware revision level for an alphastation 500 is 5.0. 
>When I turn on the machine, the console says:
>	EB164 Console V4.4-1, built on Dec 19 1995
	^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
You may have purchased an AlphaStation 500/333 but you have received
an EB164.  Nothing wrong with that, but its not a maverick, and the
maverick firmware won't work with it.  You need the eb164/pc164
firmware. 

There **may** be firmware on the firmware CD-ROM for the EB164, or
PC164  (or AlphaPC 164, or something like that).  They don't list this
firmware on their ftp site.  But I've heard there is a directory for
it on the latest firmware update CD-ROM (even though its NOT mentioned
in the docs which come with that CD-ROM).

It would be great if somebody from DEC would make a statement about
whether or not the eb164/pc164 firmware will be on future firmware
update CD-ROMS.

Thanks,

Drew



