In article <54aplp$1c3@tripath.colosys.net>, don@colosys.net (Don Wilkerson) writes:

>It's been a while since I've done this, but after I've installed a
>second SCSI card to my Alpha 1000 what do I need to put in the config
>file so the second controller is recognized and the corresponding disks.

I think you need a minimum of:

controller      scsi#   at *   vector scsiintr

where # is the next number after the highest numbered "scsi"
entry you have, and:

bus             psiop#  at pci?         vector psiopintr

or:

bus             pza#    at pci?         vector pzaintr

Use the "psiop" for the KZPAA and "pza" for the KZPSA.  Again
you'll need to fill in the right number for the '#' in each.
You shouldn't need any disk or tape lines, the SCSI driver
will figure it out for you.

Once upon a time, I didn't mind editing the configuration file
add what was necessary, but these days, I just reboot with
genvmunix, copy it to /vmunix and build a new configuration
file scratch.  Saves having to worry about what things are
called.
