The DECUS Anniversary Award
                          for Lifetime Achievement


  The Digital Equipment Computer Users Society (DECUS) Anniversary Award
  for Lifetime Achievement was created in recognition of the 30th
  Anniversary of DECUS Europe Symposia and the 35th Anniversary of the
the
  founding of DECUS.  In the United States, the Lifetime Award will be
  presented to the DECUS members or Digital employees who have made
  outstanding technical contributions that have advanced the ideals of
  technical exchange and information sharing that are the core of the
DECUS
  mission.

  Award

  Five awards are possible in the United States.  Five European Awards
were
  presented at the 30th Anniversary Symposium of DECUS Europe in
Barcelona,
  Spain.  October 6-10, 1996.  The US awards will be presented at the
35th
  Anniversary Symposium in Anaheim, California, November 9-14, 1996.

  Criteria for the DECUS US Awards

  Those DECUS members and Digital employees who have contributed
  significantly over the years to the technical exchange and information
  sharing activities of DECUS are eligible for the US Lifetime
  Award.  We recognize that DECUS is an organization that is fueled
  primarily by the contributions of volunteers.  This award focuses on
  individuals whose technical achievements have been above and beyond
those
  of the normal volunteer.

  Technical contributions include one or more of the following that have
  provided a substantial benefit to DECUS members:  sessions, seminars,
  articles, library submissions or other tangible contributions.

  Nomination and Award Process

  Nominations are open to all current or former members of DECUS and
past
  and present employees of Digital Equipment Corporation who have
  participated in DECUS.

  The attached nomination form should be submitted by 1 November 1996.
  Send the nomination via email to Awards-list@decus.org.  Be sure to
  include your name, email and telephone number.

  Awards will be decided by an award panel of current and past DECUS
  leaders (designated by the DECUS US Chapter President) and
  Nancy Strecker, Vice President DECUS and Customer Programs.
^L

