Ken Reed (kenr@sed.stel.com) wrote:
: 
: Anyone know what the maximum size of a shared memory segment is under
: DEC UNIX and the maximum number of system-wide segements you can have?
: 
: A pointer to where this information is documented would be a great
: help.

sysconfig -q vm

displays the kernel tunables you may change in /etc/sysconfigtab

The following is what I've done for shared memory:

vm:
	# Number of shared memory segments in the system
	vm-mapentries=1000

	# Max task virtual size
	vm-maxvas = 1099511627776      

	# Allows task image to grow larger than physical RAM, as long
	# as you have enough swap/virtual memory.
	vm-nowait-memalloc=1

	#
	# Pre-allocating RAM for shared mem use, to avoid a bug in
	# tasks attaching >> 512Mb.
	# gh-chunks=NNN		Where NNN is 4Mb chunks that is reserved
	#			for shared memory attaches.
	#
	# gh-fail-if-no-mem=0	If gh-chunks is too small, then use std UBC RAM
	#			which is the normal scenario...



