Ken Reed wrote:
> 
> Anyone know what the maximum size of a shared memory segment is under
> DEC UNIX and the maximum number of system-wide segements you can have?

The maximum size is 2gb even though the size argument to shmget(2)
is 'size_t' - 64 bits.  The reason for the 2gb restriction is
that the shm_segsz in the shmid_ds structure is only a signed
integer.  I believe this field may be changing to a 'size_t' in
a newer standard.

The maximum number of system wide shared memory segments possible
is controlled by the shm-mni value.  You may also want to take into
consideration shm-seg which is the maximum number of segments that
a process can attach at one time.  Both of these values are within
the ipc subsystem of the /etc/sysconfigtab file.

> A pointer to where this information is documented would be a great
> help.

Look at the man page for the sysconfigtab(4) file, the sysconfig(8)
command and also the "System Tuning and Performance Management"
manual.

Pat

