Robert Scholten (scholten@physics.unimelb.edu.au) wrote:
: Hi,
: We have two Alphastations currently connected by 10Mb/sec Ethernet.  I have
: some of the drives cross-mounted via NFS, but transfer rates are horrendously
: slow.  Something like:
: 
:   time cp testfile /dev/null
: 
: where testfile is on a cross-mounted drive, gives me speeds of 40kB/sec.

If the NFS server does not support NFSv3 protocol, then you're using NFSv2
protocol, which needs manual tuning for chunk size in your /etc/fstab file
for each mount point.  If you don't set rsize/wsize it probably defaults to
512b/1024b which is the source of your poor performance.

For example:

/usr2@gis1      /gis1/usr2      nfs hard,intr,timeo=300,rsize=8192,wsize=8192,rw,bg 0 0




Curt Smith
curts@compgen.com




