	Several questions;

	1) Do both alphas ftp at high speeds to the PC?

	2) If so, how close are the two alphas to each other?

	3) If they are not close, what pieces of ethernet
		hardware (both wires and hubs/switches) are 
		between them and not between them and the
		PC?

	Since you state that they do reasonably fast transmissions to
the PC, at a guess, you have either a flakey bit of ethernet- either
because it is too long or electrically in trouble- or the two machines
are too close together.  The recent tulip cards are much less tolerant
of ethernet that is not up to standards.

	You can check what is happening on your ethernet adaptor via
the freeware monitor program, available from gatekeeper.dec.com.

	All the best,

		Peter David



