> gatekeeper.dec.com
> 
> unpacked and installed them following the instructions the files
> contain.

Whoah! Installing mtools should not involve so many problems!
It does not have to be setuid root (and should not)!

The device file which must have world access if people other than root
will use the floppy drive is /dev/fd0c. Use the command:
--
chmod 666 /dev/fd0c
--
After doing the basic make and install, with no modifications required,
you should install the configuration file, /etc/mtools.conf
All of my machines with floppy drives, Alphastation 200's, uses the
following mtools.conf:
--
drive a: file="/dev/fd0c"
        fat_bits=12
        tracks=80 heads=2 sectors=18
        nodelay
--
The man pages which are automatically installed, describe the
configuration file: use 'man 5 mtools'.
If it's useful to you, I can repeat these instructions in German.

Cheers,

Matt
