----------------------------------------------------------------------------
             Instructions for adding anonymous ftp to OSF.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 1:
   Use the "adduser" utility to add a new user called ftp.
   The new user, ftp, should belong to the group ftp.  When
   prompted for the group that ftp should be in, answer ftp.
   Adduser will then prompt you if it should create the new
   group, answer "yes".  The new user, ftp, should have a home
   directory of /usr. The default shell is fine, you will be
   modifying it.

   The new passwd should be set to "anonymous".

   After the adduser script has run, the newly created account
   has an entry in the /etc/passwd file such as:

   
   ftp:mEFyvztssXGZk:269:79:anonymous ftp:/usr/ftp:/bin/csh

   The encoded passwd and uid will most likey be different at your
   site.

   Next, edit /etc/passwd and modify the new users login shell for
   /usr/ucb/ftp. The changed entry will look like:

   ftp:mEFyvztssXGZk:269:79:anonymous ftp:/usr/ftp:/usr/ucb/ftp

Step 2:
   Now that you have created the new ftp account, you will need
   to setup some new directories in it.

   1) cd /usr/ftp
   2) mkdir etc pub (if bin does not exist, the create it)
   3) cp /sbin/ls /usr/ftp/bin
   4) cp /etc/passwd /usr/ftp/etc
   5) cp /etc/group /usr/ftp/etc
   6) cp /etc/svc.conf /usr/ftp/etc
   7) chown -R ftp *
   8) chown ftp /usr/ftp
   9) chmod -w /usr/ftp
   10) chmod 111 /usr/ftp/bin/ls
   11) chmod -w /usr/ftp/bin
   12) chmod 444 /usr/ftp/etc
   13) chmod -w /usr/ftp/etc
   14) chmod 777 /usr/ftp/pub (this will enable writing)

Step 3:
   This concludes the anonymous ftp setup.  Any files that you wish the
   public to read will go in /usr/ftp/pub.

Step 4: 

   Testing:

   ftp to the host that you just created the anonymous ftp account:

   In my example, my hosts is called twonix.

   csh>ftp twonix
   Connected to nodename.cxo.dec.com.
   220 nodename.cxo.dec.com FTP server (Version 4.1 Sun Mar 25 18:16:27 EST
   1990) ready.
   Name (nodename::username): anonymous
   Password:anonymous
   230 Guest login ok, access restrictions apply.
   ftp>cd pub
   ftp>   


    
Please contact the Customer Support Center if you have any questions on this
procedure or need further assistance in any way.

Thankyou.
    


