Steve VanDevender wrote:
> Has anyone successfully used the getprpwent()/putprpwent() routines to
> manipulate the auth.db database, or have other experience relevant to
> using or converting shadow passwd files to work under Digital UNIX?

There are multiple solutions (under v4.0[a]), two of which are:
(1) Look at the getespwent(3) man page carefully.  Unfortunately there
    isn't a man page for the copyespwent() function referenced in 
    getespwent(3).
(2) use convauth to convert auth.db to /tcb/files/auth/?/<account> files
    then use the getprpwent/putprpwent functions
    then use convauth to convert back to auth.db format.

