Has Digital fixed the VM system in 4.0 to allocate memory to processes from
the total virtual memory allowed, less some slack space, rather than either
not allocating at all or preallocating swap only? When systems had little real
memory it made sense to approximate (total VM == swap), but today we have
systems with hundreds of megabytes and it's unrealistic to allocate a
gigabyte of swap on a system with only a couple of gig total disk space.
