OMNIBACKUP from HP, to Quantum DLT 4000 drives.  In order to get this to work,
we have to modify the vendor id on the Quantum drive so it looks like an STK
4280HP drive.  This is a pain, because we have to have the application to
modify the vendorid, and document this special case, and makes our DRP recovery
more complicated for no good reason.  It would be much nicer to use a generic
drive.

	The other problem with it is that we have our maintenance contract for
all our tape drives with DEC, and lots of the DEC DLT drives, and just a few 
of these Quantum drives.  Any time one needs to be repaired, it is a pain to
get a replacement drive because they are always out of stock or whatever. 
Our local DEC guys keep one spare for us, but we had two go out about a month
ago, and had to do without for weeks for a replacement.

	What I would really like to do is drive a DEC DLT directly from
the HP system.  I have tried installing the DLT support patch from HP, but it
doesn't work with the DEC drives, only the HP ones.  I have tried modifying
the DEC drives' vendorid to STK, but that doesn't seem to work.  I understand
that the DEC drives have some other firmware differences from the generic
Quantum drives.

	Does anybody know how to get the DEC DLT drives to be recongnized by
HP Omniback?  I heard a rumor somewhere that DEC has a patch for HP that 
allows their drives to be recognized.  Can anybody give me the name of this
patch, and any details about it I would need to know?
 
