greenwoodde@feda01.fed.ornl.gov (Dave Greenwood) writes:

> 
> We just upgraded one of our workstations to DU 4.0A and the new CDE.  When
> we invoke IDL (using an HP or a VMS system as the client) and the DU 4.0A
> workstation as the server, we're getting "Cannot allocate colormap entry for
> #xxxx" messages.  In at least one case the result is that button labels
> (and even the buttons themselves) are invisible.
> 
> Does anyone have experience with solving this problem with DU 4.0 and
> IDL 4.0[.1]?

Unless you spring for a fancy graphics card supporting 24 bit color,
you are limited to 256 colors allocated at any moment. Many uilities
map colors that may not be in use. Netscape pretty much takes whatever
is not nailed down, for example. Editors (emacs) and many other tools
take a few. CDE takes a buch for backgrounds and decorations.

You need to either go to a 24bit color card or try to tune your apps
to use the same colors. (This is a real pain.)  Please note that this
is a hardware issue not specific to any vendor.
-- 
