Several people have asked, in recent weeks, for a description
of the appropriate Digital UNIX kernel tuning parameters for use
with busy Web servers.  As it happens, we were working on producing
just such a document, and the first version has now been posted
on our Web site:
    http://www.digital.com/info/internet/document/ias/tuning.html

From the introduction:

  Digital UNIX Tuning Parameters for Web Servers

     Digital Equipment Corporation
     Maynard, Massachusetts 

     Version 1.0, October, 1996 

    The recommendations in this document result from our experience with the
    use of Digital UNIX on a variety of busy web servers, including
    altavista.digital.com.  As the information is refined and as new data
    becomes available, Digital will update this document.  Your comments
    and suggestions on this material is welcome.  Please mail your comments
    to ias-support@digital.com. 

As it says, we'd welcome your comments and suggestions regarding
this document.  Please do NOT send them to me; use the address
given in the document (since I'm not the primary author).

Note that we did not try to provide an extremely detailed document,
and we did not try to describe how to tune things exactly for every
situation.  Our goal was to suggest settings appropriate to a busy
server with an adequate amount of memory, and in some situations
you may need to experiment with different values.

-Jeff



