Matthew R. Willis wrote:
> 
> Does anyone know what the output field format is for the following
> command in Digital/UNIX OSF1:
> 
>         vmstat 5 5
> 
> Specifically what information is in each field of the output, and
> what are the units of the output (KB or blocks).

The man page describes what each field means.  The actual value
will be displayed if it is < 1000; otherwise it will appended
with a K, M, or G if larger than 1000, million or billion respectively.

I realize that 1K is actually 1024, but the intent is to fit as much
information in as little room as possible.  I suppose this stems from
the command's heritage and that it was written when output was
restricted to 80 columns.

