Rodrigo Villablanca wrote:
> 
> Hi.
> Anybody knows how can i set up the system, so it can run more process?
> I think it's a kernel option?
> I'm using OSF 3.2

If you want to allow more processes *per* *user*, then use sysconfig.
'sysconfig -q proc' shows you the values currently in place. You'll have
to alter them and reboot.

If you want to allow more processes on the system overall, you'll have
to rebuild the kernel, adding a line like:
	maxproc 1000
into the kernel configuration file.

Cheers,

