mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1
x-mailer: Mozilla 3.0b6 (X11; I; OSF1 V3.0 alpha)


Greetings to all -

  Have anyone got any experience with PLP (V.4.0.3) ?

  First I tried to compile PLP under DUnix 4.0 with no success.  
  Compiling with DUnix 3.2C was no problem, but sometime occured a
  problem with the printing. 

  We have an HPIII Si, which is connected to an terminal server
  (ET4000). Transfering the data to the terminal server is done by LAT. 
  I used latsetup to create some terminals which I configured with
  latcp -A -p tty02 -H ts -R HP3_POSTSCRIPT.

  Problems:
  1. Invoking the lpr command, while the status (lpq) is "closing" 
     cause the lpd to stop this queue (no daemon present).    
  
  2. Sometimes the printer (queue ?) is in a funny state: All looks like 
     normal: File is active, printer indicates receiving data by 
     flashing a LED ... but there is no output.
     After an hardware reset on the printer I can sent the same file and 
     I got the correct output.

  printcap entries:
    #
    # printing via LAT on HP3PS: Postscript, einseitig
    #
    pit3ps|hp3ps|HP3PS|pit_ps|PIT_PS:\
        :cm=HP LaserJet IIISi, PS einseitig:\
        :ct=LAT:\
        :br#19200:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lpd/lp_pit3ps:\
        :lp=/dev/tty02:\
        :fe=/usr/spool/filter/pit3ps-filter:\
        :mx#0:\
        :sh:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/pit3ps:
    #
    # remote printing on HP3PS: Postscript doppelseitig:
    #
    pit3dps|hp3dps:\
        :cm=HP LaserJet IIISi, PS doppelseitig:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lpd/lp_pit3dps:\
        :lp=:\
        :if=/usr/spool/filter/pit3dps-filter:\
        :rm=piosf7:rp=pit3ps:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/pit3dps:

  pit3(d)ps-filter:
    #! /bin/sh
    /bin/sed -f/usr/spool/filter/ps_pit3(d)ps
  ps_pit3ps:
    1{
    i\
    ^[%-12345X@PJL ENTER LANGUAGE = PostScript
    }
  ps-pit3dps:
    1{
    i\
    statusdict begin true setduplexmode end
    }

  I also tried to use the DUnix lpd daemon instead of plp, but I had
  no success to make the "pit3dps" (double side mode) queue working.
  The normal "pit3ps" queue (one page mode) worked fine (more or less).
  Thanks in advance for any help or hints.

 Uwe Siodlaczek
 siodlaczek@pit.physik.uni-tuebingen.de



