birgitt boersch-Pulm wrote:
> 
> Hallo,
> 
> I try to install mtools 3.0 on an Alpha workstation under
> DIGITAL UNIX V3.2C
> 
> The installation seems to be o.k., but it doesn't work.
> 
> error message :
> 
> # ./mdir
> Drive 'A:' not supported
> Cannot initialize 'A:'
> 
> when I try to insert in devices.c something like :
> 
> #ifdef alpha
> #define predefined_devices
> struct device devices[] = {
>         {"/dev/rfd0c",  'A', GENFD},
>         {"/dev/rfd0c", 'A', HD514},
>         {"/dev/rfd0c", 'A', DD514},
> };
> #endif
> 
> and restart make, I get the following error message:
> 
> Unresolved:
> init_geom
> *** Exit 1
> Stop.
> 

Add this to devices.c

< #ifdef ALPHASTATION
< struct device devices[] = {
<       {'A', "/dev/rfd0c", 0L, 12, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 80, 2, 18},
<       {'A', "/dev/rfd0a", 0L, 12, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 80, 2, 9},
<       {'\0', (char *) NULL, 0L, 0, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 0, 0, 0}
< };
< #endif /* ALPHASTATION */

Add this to Makefile

> # for AlphaStation
> CFLAGS = -O -DALPHASTATION -DLOCKF

It works for me on DU 3.2C.
